<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Olinda</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Olinda is a colonial town on the coast of Pernambuco, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, founded in 1535 by the donatary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duarte-coelho">Duarte Coelho</a> as the capital of his captaincy. Rich from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a>, it was captured and burned by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> in 1631, who favoured the nearby port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/recife">Recife</a>. Its hilltop churches and convents form a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/olinda.jpg" alt="Olinda" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Valdiney Pimenta · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Convento_de_S%C3%A3o_Francisco_-_Olinda_-_Pernambuco_-_Brasil.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
